WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.610
How far are we gonna fall?

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.040
It's like a slide!

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.730
Where is this taking us?!

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.240
Don't ask me!

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.170
We're saved.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.280
Ow...

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.500
You guys...

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.250
Oh... Liang and Upa?

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.250
Ouch!

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.250
I just bumped into you a little.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.290
I was just...

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.130
I didn't land directly on you!

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.620
Why the hell are you here?!

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:56.490
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:05.980
<b>You Are Weak</b>

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.610
Hey, what the heck are you doing here?

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.910
That's my line!

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.350
You guys are the ones who fell in!

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.650
Is this your cell room, Master?

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.160
Of course not.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.230
As you can clearly see, we're restrained.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.340
It's a bit complicated.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.560
In any case, why did you 
guys come to Building 5?

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.140
Well, Rock was kinda acting weird,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.730
and he had some talisman-looking
thing on his neck.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:26.500
What?

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.030
I heard it's from here,

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:31.050
so we came to check.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:31.960
Shh.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.980
Be quiet for a moment.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.730
Don't make noise carelessly, 
or you'll lose your head.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.550
Huh? What? What's wrong?

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.100
You shouldn't look.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.220
It'll probably be a shock to you, Uno-kun.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.080
What? A girl? Is there a girl?

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.240
You definitely shouldn't look.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.620
That's the surveillance doll for
Building 5's former underground cell.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.450
They made a scary thing like that here?

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.910
No, it didn't originate at this prison.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:16.630
It was used in the prison where
we were previously held.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:20.660
He brought it here to keep an eye on us.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.010
He?

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.010
<b>Underground Level 5</b>

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:28.390
Thanks for being an obedient 
captive, Sugoroku.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.270
But then again, even you know 
what those cuffs can do, right?

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.600
I knew it right away.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.280
It's one of the special items he brought here.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:46.490
If you try to break it or apply any 
kind of impact, it will explode.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:51.040
It's powerful enough to blow both 
your hands off, so be careful.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.990
See ya, Sugoroku.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.380
Let's see...

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.560
What to do now?

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.140
He took all my communication devices,

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.600
and I'm in the underground cell,
which is no longer in use.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.310
The surveillance cameras are dead...

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.140
And I'm in these pain-in-the-ass cuffs.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:10.990
What should I do?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.650
Talk about pitiful, Hajime.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.340
Look at you, locked in a cage...

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.290
How very fitting.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.530
He actually unlocked them!

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.160
Isn't he awesome?!

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.040
This guy can unlock anything!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.790
Why are <i>you</i> bragging about that?

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.860
Anyway, who did you mean by "he" earlier?

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:40.470
Is he the one who locked us up here?

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.700
I guess it won't be a problem if we tell you guys.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.780
Can we make our move soon?

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:52.200
I took care of everyone who was in the way.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.690
I apologize for taking a while, but...

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:58.920
"A while," my ass.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.440
Big oafs like you are so slow. 
It's such a hassle.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:05.700
I would've taken care of it a lot faster.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.280
Shut up, you damn kappa!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.620
I'm the one who got you out of the cell!

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:12.080
I'm the one who gave you advice.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.580
Stop wasting your breath.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.460
I don't have time.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.460
An inmate escaped from Building 5.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.710
Escaped?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.970
He's a former supervising 
officer for this building.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:29.640
His name is Enki Gokuu.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:31.970
Let's go.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.680
Yes. He's Samon-san's brother,

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.730
though they're nothing alike.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:43.120
He used to work at the 
Chinese prison we were in.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.620
He cruelly beat many inmates there,

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:51.340
but he wasn't doing it 
out of anger or hatred.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:56.500
To him, the inmates were nothing but training
dummies he could use to get stronger.

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:03.150
There were many times I thought
that I would be killed.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.430
When he was transferred to Nanba Prison,

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.470
I was truly relieved.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.840
But I heard he continued to be 
cruel to the inmates here, as well.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:14.450
But he was a supervisor, right?

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.420
Why was he imprisoned?

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.520
Did he do something that bad?

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.520
He ended up killing an inmate.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.640
Killed... an inmate?

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:27.100
A correctional officer?

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.380
I didn't see it with my own eyes.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.250
I only heard rumors.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.890
But I wouldn't be surprised if he did.

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:38.890
He was already imprisoned by 
the time we were sent here.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.180
What?!

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:42.790
And you're telling me he escaped?!

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.050
Hey, what are you doing?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.550
Hurry up.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.420
Y-Yes, sir...

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.140
No one could stop him...

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.310
Not even Samon-san.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:07.070
This Enki guy, what does he 
intend to accomplish by escaping?

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.380
Who knows?

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:11.540
But letting us live would 
serve no purpose for him.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.820
He may kill us when he feels the time is right.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:17.120
Hey, how can you say something 
that pessimistic so calmly?!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.300
If you know that, let's get outta here!

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.100
If we could get out, 
we would've done it already.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.080
This is a special cell.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.120
Qigong won't work on it, 
and it's unbreakable.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.840
Resistance is futile.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.970
Whatever, let's just get going!

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.390
What?!

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:37.220
Hey, Nico. What are you doing? Let's go.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:40.230
Gone... It's gone!

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:41.860
What are you looking for?

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.550
I lost my medicine bag...

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.500
What?! Seriously?!

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.480
Jyugo-kun, can you look for it with me?

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.320
Yeah, okay!

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.740
Speaking of which, where's that other guy?

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.490
That tall dude.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:00.000
Who cares about that trash?

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:10.680
Taking your sweet time, aren't you, Mr. Rookie?

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.590
Do you wanna be imprisoned, too?

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:17.260
You'll be the one to suffer if you don't wise up.

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:22.230
Isn't it cool? I found it earlier.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.980
I wonder what's inside it...

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:33.990
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.120
<b>A few hours earlier</b>

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:47.250
They're here.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:48.330
And here...

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:53.260
I've never miscounted the 
talismans before now.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:56.760
It doesn't seem like

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.510
any were taken from here, either.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:06.170
But they're definitely gone.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:07.180
Supervisor!

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.150
I told you not to come in here.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.530
I-It's an emergency!

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:14.780
An inmate has escaped!

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.600
What do you mean?! Who escaped?!

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:23.520
Inmate Number 5900...

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.560
Enki Gokuu!

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.290
Why didn't you report this immediately?!

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:33.550
It seems like someone's messed with 
the communication system.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:37.810
<i>There's no way he could pull a stunt 
like that while incarcerated.</i>

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:42.870
<i>It's physically impossible to escape from 
the underground cell in the first place.</i>

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.680
Did someone help him?

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:47.690
I hate to say it, but probably.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:51.570
Got it. I'll stop him one way or another.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:53.070
Please wait!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.620
There are two others...

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.320
There are three escapees!

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.980
What?

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:02.200
One is a former guard, Ruka Gojyou...

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:06.080
The other is a former boss of an
assassin organization, Inmate Number 8.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.320
They escaped from the underground cell, too?!

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:14.090
I think it's impossible for us to 
apprehend all three of them, sir.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:17.760
Since our communications are cut off,

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:22.220
I think we should go to headquarters 
and request backup first.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.870
We don't have time for that!

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.850
But you can't go alone, sir.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.560
You'll be up against Enki-san!

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:34.610
Are you saying that I can't handle him?

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:40.750
I'm not gonna let something 
like that happen again.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.800
Never again...

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:21.570
Hey, if it isn't Samon-kun.

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:24.640
The water feels good here.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.830
Underground is so dusty. I hated it.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.000
Gojyou...

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:33.760
I never would've thought there was a 
huge garden like this right above us.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:35.300
We kinda went crazy,

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:37.490
so it looks a little different now, though.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:40.340
How did you escape from underground?

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:45.470
Why don't you ask the person behind you?

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.850
You didn't notice my chi?

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:55.360
I guess this is the best you can do.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:56.860
Samon,

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:58.940
you are weak.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:08.400
Step aside.

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:12.250
Brother... Why do you want to leave here?

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.980
You don't need to know.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:17.840
If you get in my way, I'll kill you.

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:23.330
What I'm about to do is inconceivable to you.

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:26.450
Are you gonna repeat what you did that day?

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:27.760
What if I am?

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.110
<i>Though I may have my doubts,</i>

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:32.980
<i>I have to stop him somehow.</i>

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.020
<i>Otherwise...</i>

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:39.310
<i>I'll feel the same humiliation 
and regret all over again.</i>

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:40.900
<i>I can't let that happen!</i>

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.330
Oh, my. He's gonna do it.

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:45.640
He intends to catch us again.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.870
Damn right I do!

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.590
What prison guard wouldn't 
apprehend escaped convicts?!

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:51.160
Huh?

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:54.420
You think you're a bigshot supervisor now?

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:57.170
You talk big for someone who has no talent.

00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:02.450
Becoming a supervisor in the commotion
while Enki-san was being imprisoned...

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:04.930
That must've felt good.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:08.210
I really hated you from the start.

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:10.990
It's obvious you're no match for Enki-san,

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:14.940
and yet people respected you so much 
just because you were his brother.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.440
A lot of people were unhappy about that.

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:23.510
In here, only a person with 
absolute power should be served.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:27.660
After Enki-san was gone from Building 5,
people couldn't stand working under you.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.150
You were one of them, right?

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.440
Inori...

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:37.970
Huh?

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:39.580
What the hell are you doing?!

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.240
What am I doing?

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:45.040
You can't tell? I'm on their side.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.800
Huh? Is that odd?

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.800
I've said all along that I hate working, right?

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:54.480
I don't really care about
what Gojyou's saying,

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:58.350
but even I know the undeniable 
difference between you and Enki-san.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:03.000
You haven't changed at all since that day.

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:13.860
Samon, what are you doing?!

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:15.750
This is due to misconduct in your building!

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.370
Monkey! You have to do it!

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:27.510
The deputy supervisor who handled things
in your place was promoted to supervisor

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:30.720
after the incident in recognition of his skill.

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:35.970
It must be very frustrating for you.

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.820
I get why you're always 
snippy with Sugoroku

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:41.280
and how you're desperate to surpass him.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:44.410
But your inner self, the essential 
part, hasn't changed at all.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.360
I've had it with working for someone like you.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:53.560
So you're the one who messed with the 
communication system and let these guys out.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:56.590
Indeed. It was all me.

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:59.250
How long have you been 
communicating with them?

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:01.040
From the beginning.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.480
Since Enki-san was imprisoned.

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:06.590
You don't see anything but yourself.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.510
That's why a low-ranking officer 
like me could trick you.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.110
How pathetic.

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:16.020
I knew you weren't capable 
of taking Enki-san's place.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.020
Your sights are set on 
something totally different.

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:25.800
This is goodbye, Supervisor.

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:29.030
Thanks for everything.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:35.030
And I'm in these pain-in-the-ass cuffs.

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:38.040
I thought they got rid of these.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.950
What should I do?

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.250
Talk about pitiful, Hajime.

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:47.110
Look at you, locked in a cage...

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:48.870
How very fitting.

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:50.800
You're one to talk, monkey.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.430
Shut up! Don't call me monkey!

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:56.870
Damn, I wanna punch you so bad right now...

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.930
But I can't even move my fingers anymore.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.940
What's going on in Building 5 right now?

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:05.720
He escaped from the underground cell.

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:07.330
So that's it.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:09.620
I had a feeling that was what happened.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:12.570
He's the one who made this former 
underground cell, after all.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:17.200
I tried to stop him this time.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:18.820
But...

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:21.230
You hesitated again, didn't you?

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:22.460
One question.

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.420
Enki made these, right?

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.960
Why do they still exist?

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:30.180
I thought they got rid of all these.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:33.680
You hid them, didn't you?

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.720
Well, that doesn't matter. 
But I'll tell you one thing.

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:41.400
He's a criminal. Don't forget that.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:42.740
I know that...

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:43.730
No, you don't!

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.420
If you really intend to stop Enki...

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.200
Next time, kill him if you must.

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:02.840
All right! These stairs go up.

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:05.510
We should be able to reach 
the surface by going up here.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:07.130
Let's hurry!

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:11.720
Hey, Jyugo, what're you doing?

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:14.010
Isn't this Hajime's?

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.010
<b>Sugoroku</b>

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:17.540
You're right.

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:19.270
Why is it here?

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:21.880
Hajime was caught on the surface, wasn't he?

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:24.070
Let's head up for now.

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:24.730
No...

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:26.780
We're not going up.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.210
Huh? Why not?

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.700
Shouldn't we hurry up and get out of here?

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:32.360
You idiot.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:36.240
These underground cells usually 
have heavy security near the exits.

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:38.940
Once they find out we escaped,

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:41.740
they'll tighten security at the 
exit passageway even more.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.300
You've got a point there.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:45.760
And even if we do escape to the outside,

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.170
what happens next?

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:48.500
Whatever the reason,

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.790
we're still considered escapees,

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.670
and they'll extend our prison terms.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:56.910
I see... That would burden Samon-san, too.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.670
So what are we gonna do?

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:00.140
Are we just gonna stay here?

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:01.480
No way.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:04.060
All we need to do is make sure 
we don't get out by ourselves.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:07.960
Hajime and the Building 5 supervisor 
are captured too, right?

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:11.280
So we just need to escape with them.

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:12.290
With them?

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.840
With their strength,

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.020
we'll be able to break 
through the exit's security,

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.780
and we won't be treated like escaped 
convicts if we stick with them.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:21.970
Using the guards as bodyguards...

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:24.180
How do you come up with this stuff?

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:27.340
At a time like this, we have 
to use any means necessary.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:31.420
Besides, they're obligated to
supervise us in the first place.

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:35.630
Even so, isn't Hajime on the surface?

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:36.420
Idiot!

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:42.190
Why is his name badge here, then?

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:44.500
It's natural to think he was 
captured on the surface

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.300
and brought somewhere down here, right?

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:47.660
That's right.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:51.360
This underground cell was 
specially created by Enki.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.600
It's impossible for even
the guards to escape from.

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:56.940
But how are we going to find him 
when we have no idea where he is?

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.560
We're gonna go look for him.

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:02.320
You're essential to this plan.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:03.410
You'd better keep up.

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.140
This place is bigger than I thought.

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:14.150
We've only been to the Gogyousan Underground
Cell once before, to organize equipment,

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:17.090
but I heard it has five levels.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:21.900
And those creepy surveillance 
dolls are on every level?

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:27.100
<b>Underground Level 1</b>

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:23.600
What's a surveillance doll?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:25.680
They're machines,

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.340
so they can't detect human presence.

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:30.760
We'll be all right as long as we're cautious.

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:32.620
Hey, what are you guys talking about?

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:35.800
But it'll be dangerous if they 
find you, so be careful.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:40.460
They were originally created 
to manage death row inmates,

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:44.030
so they're programmed to 
kill if there's a problem.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.130
I feel so left out!

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:48.450
You guys talkin' about girls? Huh? Huh? Huh?!

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:49.860
Shh! Quiet!

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:52.080
I said, let me out!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.200
Do you hear me?! Huh?!

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:57.220
How dare you lock me up 
in a shithole like this?!

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:58.870
Screw you!

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:01.920
H-Hey, that loud, foul mouth...

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:04.220
It can't be...

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.050
I'll beat the crap out of you guys!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:09.220
That middle finger! It's definitely him!

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:12.200
They'll find us if he keeps that up.

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:14.300
We need to shut him up fast.

00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:16.380
Oh, hell...

00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:19.690
What the heck are you guys doing?

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:22.150
Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:24.580
Right back at ya.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.920
You guys belong in Building 3.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:29.440
Kiji-san told us we need to exercise a little,

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:32.660
so we got permission from 
Building 5 to be brought here.

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:34.560
But once we got here,

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:38.530
we fell into a trap, and even 
Kiji-san was captured.

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:37.460
What are you doing?! Let me go!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.850
Take your dirty hands off me!

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:39.850
It was a disaster...

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:44.930
And we ended up being locked 
up in this underground cell.

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:50.250
On top of that, there are creepy dolls 
roaming around, but not a single guard!

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.720
Just what the hell is going on?!

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:57.570
Shut it.

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:00.540
We'll let you out, so keep quiet.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:02.360
And what's this about creepy dolls?

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:05.760
I see...

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:10.740
So you think the former supervisor 
who escaped is behind all this.

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:13.600
And judging by this series of traps,

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:15.740
there's no way he did it alone.

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:18.240
He must have an accomplice.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:20.900
It's impossible for us to 
fight them on our own.

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:22.800
Our only option is to bet on the plan

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.900
that gives us a higher chance of escaping,
even if it might be reckless.

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:28.180
We can't waste any time.

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:30.140
Jeez, I guess we have no choice.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:31.940
I'm sure Hajime-chan is fine,

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:33.890
but I wonder if the other people are okay.

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:35.870
Don't be too hasty.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.350
I came up with all sorts of plans.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:42.940
All right...

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:45.480
Let's do this.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:30.430
Finding Hajime's name tag made us 
think that he'd been transferred,

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:33.930
so we descend further down into 
the Gogyousan Underground Cell.

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:36.860
But what was waiting for us down there was...

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>One's Own Freedom</b>

00:23:36.860 --> 00:23:39.240
Next episode: "One's Own Freedom."
